(* Blorp 2: scalar bindings, fixed unions, tail matches and a small input prelude.

   This is a byte-level source grammar. No whitespace is implicit.
   Dialect: `=` defines a rule; `;` ends it; juxtaposition concatenates;
   `|` means alternatives; (...) groups; [...] is zero or one occurrence;
   {...} is zero or more occurrences; quoted strings are literal bytes;
   "A".."Z" is an inclusive single-byte range; comments use parentheses
   around asterisks. X - Y excludes the complete strings of Y from X.
   Grammar literal escapes are \n = LF (0x0A), \t = TAB (0x09),
   and \" = double quote (0x22). These do not introduce source escapes.
   EOF succeeds only at the exact end of the source, consuming no byte.

   Lexical contracts:
   - Identifiers use the longest consecutive identifier byte run.
   - The exact spellings `func`, `pure`, `match`, `var`, and `_` are reserved.
     Lone `_` is a wildcard token; `_name` remains an identifier.
   - Integer tokens use the longest consecutive digit run, with an optional
     adjacent minus. Parsing rejects leading zeros and values outside
     -9223372036854775808..9223372036854775807. `-0` has value zero.
   - Plus signs, separated minus signs, floats and arithmetic are unsupported.
     A dot starts UFCS, so `42.identity()` is a call and `42.5` is invalid.
   - Arrow bytes stay adjacent. Spaces occur only where these rules permit.
   - All source bytes are ASCII; CR, comments and other bytes are unsupported.

   Syntax accepts any unreserved function, parameter and type identifier.
   `fixed` and `union` are contextual words in a union header, and remain
   valid function, type, parameter and variant identifiers elsewhere.
   The checker requires exactly one zero-parameter `main` returning `Int`.
   Helper parameter and return types are `Int`, `String`, a declared fixed union,
   or one of the function's declared rigid type parameters. Type parameters start
   with a capital ASCII letter and contain only ASCII letters and digits.
   Their names cannot collide with builtin or declared union type names.
   Every body is checked once, including unused generic declarations. Only
   all synthesized argument types consistently infer a generic call; expected result types
   do not infer it. Explicit arguments whose receiving annotations contain rigid
   parameters need already-typed union values or concrete helpers. Concrete
   explicit annotations supply constructor context even in generic contracts.
   A generic UFCS receiver receives no constructor hint, even for a concrete
   first annotation. Zero-argument and phantom
   generic calls cannot infer all their parameters. Main and runtime prelude
   declarations cannot be generic. Explicit call type arguments are deferred.
   Fixed unions may declare one type parameter. Written applications take one
   atomic argument: Int, String, an in-scope parameter or an ordinary union.
   Nested written applications are unsupported. Payload annotations are Int
   or the union's own parameter; concrete payloads must specialize to Int.
   Phantom String applications remain valid. Instance identity includes the
   declaration and complete ordered concrete arguments, independently of layout.
   Type names occupy a separate namespace from function and variant names.
   Union type names and variants within one union must be unique. Functions
   cannot share a variant name; variants in different unions may share names.
   Bare variants resolve in the expected union type, determined by the
   receiving function parameter or declared return type. A local parameter
   shadows a same-named variant or direct call and cannot be called. A UFCS
   target resolves globally, independently of parameter shadowing; its receiver
   uses the containing function's scope. Calls require matching arity and
   nominal types, acyclic edges, and pure callers calling only pure callees.
   Unannotated functions are impure. Nullary variants are bare values. A
   variant with one declared field uses unary construction syntax. Constructor
   application is pure and is not a function call; constructor UFCS is deferred.
   Matches follow any binding prefix and occupy the function tail. Their scrutinee must synthesize
   a union type from a binding or function result; a constructor alone does not
   provide a receiving type. An unshadowed constructor spelling selects that
   union's variant. Other bare names, including a spelling shadowed by a local
   binding, introduce fresh whole-value bindings. Field binders and wildcards
   are irrefutable. Checking requires
   exhaustive, useful arms and type-checks every arm result.
   Bindings resolve initializer names before adding a new local. `var`
   creates a mutable local and may shadow an enclosing binding. Ordinary `=`
   reassigns a visible mutable binding, rejects a visible immutable binding,
   or creates a new immutable local. Duplicate declarations within one block
   are rejected. New local types are inferred; reassignment retains the established
   type. Bare constructors need a receiving type. Every initializer is
   checked and evaluated, even when its binding is unused. An arm may contain
   an inline expression or a depth-three block of bindings and a final value.
   Arm-local declarations do not enter sibling scopes. Explicit var may
   shadow an enclosing binding; a second declaration in the same block fails.
   The separately supplied prelude admits only the builtin type declarations
   and runtime-backed function declarations below. It must declare Int and
   String exactly once. Names of its functions are ordinary declared names;
   the closed builtin label establishes the operation identity. Checking
   requires pure unary Int -> String for int.to_string and String -> Int for
   string.length. Program functions and variants cannot conflict with prelude
   functions. No prelude function is inserted when its declaration is absent.
   Quoted labels are not general String values and cannot appear in programs.
   Ownership admits fresh arm-local Strings in a tail match; its parameters and
   prefix must remain unmanaged. Each arm drops its unused/intermediate owners
   or transfers a String result. Managed outer dependencies and joins are deferred.
*)

letter           = "A".."Z" | "a".."z" ;
digit            = "0".."9" ;
identifier_start = letter | "_" ;
identifier_byte  = identifier_start | digit ;
identifier       = (identifier_start { identifier_byte }) - ("func" | "pure" | "match" | "var" | "_") ;

space            = " " ;
spaces           = { space } ;
required_spaces  = space spaces ;
newline          = "\n" ;
indent_one       = "\t" | "    " ;
indent_two       = "\t\t" | "        " ;
indent_three     = "\t\t\t" | "            " ;

(* A function has one header followed by zero or more binding lines and a
   mandatory expression line or tail match.
   A union has one header and one or more variant lines. A single LF
   separates declarations; the final line may omit its LF.
   Blank lines and trailing whitespace after the
   final LF are unsupported. Spaces in a call are explicit, including f ( )
   and 1 . f ( ). UFCS supplies its receiver as the first argument, followed
   by the ordered explicit arguments in its parentheses. All expressions stay on one
   line, including scrutinees and arm results. Indentation prefixes are entirely
   tabs or spaces; spaces count in groups of four. Bodies and variants require
   depth one, match arms depth two, and arm-block lines depth three.
   Blocks finish with a single-line value; no nested matches. *)
nonzero_digit    = "1".."9" ;
integer          = [ "-" ] ("0" | nonzero_digit { digit }) ;
arguments        = expression { spaces "," spaces expression } ;
direct_call      = identifier spaces "(" spaces [ arguments ] spaces ")" ;
primary          = integer | identifier | direct_call ;
receiver_call    = spaces "." spaces identifier spaces "(" spaces [ arguments ] spaces ")" ;
expression       = primary { receiver_call } ;
type_annotation  = identifier spaces [ "[" spaces identifier spaces "]" ] ;
parameter        = identifier spaces ":" spaces type_annotation ;
type_parameter   = "A".."Z" { letter | digit } ;
function_type_parameters = "[" spaces type_parameter { spaces "," spaces type_parameter } spaces "]" spaces ;
union_type_parameter = "[" spaces type_parameter spaces "]" spaces ;
function_header  = [ "pure" required_spaces ] "func" required_spaces identifier spaces [ function_type_parameters ] "(" spaces
                   [ parameter { spaces "," spaces parameter } ] spaces ")" spaces "->" spaces type_annotation spaces ":" spaces
                   newline ;
function         = function_header body ;
field_pattern    = "_" | identifier ;
pattern          = "_" | identifier spaces [ "(" spaces [ field_pattern ] spaces ")" ] ;
arm_binding      = indent_three [ "var" required_spaces ] identifier spaces "=" spaces expression spaces ;
arm_block        = { arm_binding newline } indent_three expression spaces ;
match_arm        = indent_two pattern spaces ":" spaces
                   (expression spaces | newline arm_block) ;
match_body       = indent_one "match" required_spaces expression spaces ":" spaces
                   newline match_arm { newline match_arm } ;
binding          = indent_one [ "var" required_spaces ] identifier spaces "=" spaces expression spaces ;
tail             = indent_one expression spaces | match_body ;
body             = { binding newline } tail ;
variant          = indent_one identifier spaces [ "(" spaces identifier spaces ")" spaces ] ;
fixed_union      = "fixed" required_spaces "union" required_spaces identifier spaces [ union_type_parameter ] ":" spaces
                   newline variant { newline variant } ;
declaration      = function | fixed_union ;
program          = declaration { newline declaration } [ newline ] EOF ;

(* The prelude uses the same lexical and header rules as the input program.
   An empty prelude parses but fails the required builtin-type checks. *)
builtin_type     = "type" required_spaces ("Int" | "String") spaces "=" spaces "builtin" spaces ;
builtin_label    = "\"int.to_string\"" | "\"string.length\"" ;
runtime_function = function_header indent_one "builtin" spaces "(" spaces builtin_label spaces ")" spaces ;
prelude_declaration = builtin_type | runtime_function ;
prelude          = [ prelude_declaration { newline prelude_declaration } [ newline ] ] EOF ;
